        "content": "<p>pujitha24 opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14956\">PR #14956</a> from <code>pujitha24:auto/issue-14945</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14945\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14945</a></p>\n<p>On aarch64, an <code>i128</code> argument that doesn't fit in the remaining integer registers goes on the stack, but the next-register counter wasn't advanced. A following <code>i64</code> was then assigned to <code>x7</code>. AAPCS64 C.13 (and clang/gcc, including on Darwin) pass it on the stack. This sets the counter to 8 in that case, for <code>system_v</code> and <code>apple_aarch64</code> arguments only.</p>\n<p>Cranelift-to-Cranelift calls were self-consistent, so this only affects signatures shared with C/Rust code. Wasmtime doesn't pass <code>i128</code> across calls.</p>\n<p>Testing: new cases in <code>isa/aarch64/call.clif</code> (previously compiled to <code>mov x0, x7</code>, now a stack load). The aarch64 and runtests filetest directories pass.</p>\n<p>Disclosure: I used an AI tool (Claude) to help prepare this change.</p>\n<p>This PR was written in part with the assistance of generative AI.</p>\n<p>Fixes #14945</p>\n</blockquote>",
